// Scalar-unification: the TWO unified bundle constraints reject a mismatched target at the `impl`
// site (E0015), the compile-time twin of the runtime shape check. `vec.Kernels` (AnyNumeric,
// Uniform {min: 2}) rejects a `bool` vector and a 1-field struct; `vec.SatKernels` (AnyInteger)
// additionally rejects a FLOAT vector — saturating math is integer-only, so a float shape has no
// saturating mode. (Under the old three-bundle world an f32 vector, a 4×i32 shape, and a 3×u8 shape
// were all impl-site errors; now they bind — the whole point of the collapse — so the surviving
// rejections are these genuinely-invalid shapes.)
// expect: error E0015 at 19:22
// expect: error E0015 at 20:22
// expect: error E0015 at 21:25
// expect: error E0015 at 22:25
// expect: exit 1
use std.{vec}

@packed struct One { x: i32 }
@packed struct Flags { a: bool; b: bool }
@packed struct FVec3 { x: f32; y: f32; z: f32 }

impl vec.Kernels for One {}
impl vec.Kernels for Flags {}
impl vec.SatKernels for FVec3 {}
impl vec.SatKernels for One {}
